# A reference reaches a formal only through a call that runs (review169
# check lens): reads(p) inside c.sizeof never runs, so p is received by no
# formal there and its used scope has no edge from reads. The one receiving
# of p is its own typed declaration. Success is 7.
Box: (int: a; int: b)
fn: reads (Box: x) int
    return: x\a
end: reads
fn: quiet () int
    @: p Box Box
    size_t: r c.sizeof(reads(p))
    if: r != c.sizeof(c.int)
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: quiet
Box\a: 3
if: quiet() != 7
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 80; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
